 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 529841,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Identify the mean and standard deviation of this distribution. Anything within 5 on the standard deviation is acceptable.<br>\n<figure>\n<img src=\"exercises/media/51e6870d56ef7591.png\" alt=\"A normal distribution curve. The horizontal axis ranges from 80 to 200, in increments of 5. The curve begins at 80, has a peak value at 150, and ends at 200.\">\n</figure>",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>Step 1:Draw a line down from the peak. It could help you to hold an index card up to the screen. Have one edge along the horizontal axis and the other edge going through the peak. Read the position of the card on the horizontal axis. It will tell you the mean is 150.</p>\n<p>Step 2: Starting from the peak, notice where the curve changes from curving down to curving up. Mark the point where that curvature changes, the inflection point. Draw a line down from that point. You can use your index card again to help you judge where the inflection point falls.</p>\n<p>It looks like the inflection point is around 170.</p>\n<p>Step 3: The distance between the two lines along the horizontal axis is an estimate of the standard deviation.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"170 - 150 = 20\"></span></p>\n<p>The standard deviation is 20.</p>\n<p>You might have been off a bit because of the difficulty of judging where the inflection point is.</p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "Mean: 150; standard deviation: 20"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
